<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Pump emulation model for the Jde OpcServer and the PLC emulator (apps/OpcServer/emulator).
  Loaded by both processes via /opcServer/configFiles and /emulator/plc/nodeset so the emulated PLC's address space
  mirrors the server's.  PumpType.status is the run command (written by the UI, subscribed by the emulator);
  PumpType.motorRpm is the process value the emulator publishes (config/pubsub/pumps.libsonnet lists the fields).
  NodeSet2 does not instantiate types, so every pump declares its own status/motorRpm variables.

  The variables marked Historizing="true" are the ones the OpcServer keeps the history of (libs/historian/docs/spec.md,
  *OpcServer*), each under the thresholds of its HA Configuration object.  Between them they cover every
  ExceptionDeviationFormat, a MinTimeInterval and a MaxTimeInterval, the heartbeat, against the emulator's signals:
    pump1.status        no HA Configuration - the server adds one, with the defaults: every change is stored.
    pump1.motorRpm      5 rpm, ABSOLUTE_VALUE (0), at most one value a second (MinTimeInterval).
    pump2.motorRpm      1 PERCENT_OF_VALUE (1), re-stored every minute it holds still (MaxTimeInterval).
    pump3.motorRpm      1 PERCENT_OF_RANGE (2) of its InstrumentRange, 0-1500: 15 rpm.
    pump4.motorRpm      0.5 PERCENT_OF_EU_RANGE (3) of its EURange, 0-3000: 15 rpm.
    pumpManual.motorRpm 10, with no format: the server adds ABSOLUTE_VALUE.
  The PLC emulator loads the file too and keeps no history: there the attribute and the objects are only nodes.
-->
